3. How to upload your project to GitHub
Getting Started with GitHub
 
Step 1: Create a GitHub repository

Visit GitHub  and sign in. Click the New repository option.

Use GitHub with GitHub Desktop | o7planning.org
 
Step 2: Repository name

Enter HTML-Foundations-Mini-Project, select Public, and click Create repository.

What Is GitHub? Ultimate Guide on How to Use GitHub in 2025
 
Step 3: Upload your HTML file

Click Add file → Upload files. Select your index.html file and upload it.

GitHub - yining1023/ml4w-homework
 
Step 4: Commit your code

Enter the commit message Added personal introduction webpage and click Commit changes.

4. Alternative: Upload using Git commands
If you have Git installed, open the terminal inside your project folder and run:


bash
git init
git add index.html
git commit -m "Added personal introduction webpage"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/HTML-Foundations-Mini-Project.git
git push -u origin main
Replace YOUR-USERNAME with your actual GitHub username.

